${"##"} Sleep retention

Conditions: "pad" is MIO pad `p` or DIO pad `d`; "status bit" is its bit in `MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS` or `DIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS`; "sleep entry" is a rise of `sleep_en_i`.
The mode rows hold while no TAP owns the pad and the sleep mode is unchanged since sleep entry.

Testpoints: `pad_sleep` (V2, priority 2), `sleep_release` (V2, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_SLP_01 | At sleep entry, the status bit of every pad whose sleep enable is 1 shall become 1, unless a software clear of that bit lands in the same cycle (`REQ_SLP_09`). | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_EN.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_en); [Sleep Features](../programmers_guide.md#sleep-features) | `pad_sleep`: *bit set at entry* | For every sleep entry with the pad's sleep enable at 1 and no software clear of its status bit, the check requires the bit to be 1 in the next cycle. A bit that stays 0, or rises a cycle late, fails it; a cycle with a clear is decided by _clear wins_ (CHK_PAD_SLEEP_05). |
| REQ_SLP_02 | A status bit shall become 1 only at sleep entry, and only if the pad's sleep enable is 1. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_status${on(topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split(), '_0')}); [Sleep Features](../programmers_guide.md#sleep-features) | `pad_sleep`: *bit set only at entry* | For every rise of a status bit the check requires a sleep entry with the pad's sleep enable at 1 in the cycle before. A bit that rises with the enable at 0, without a rise of `sleep_en_i`, or while `sleep_en_i` merely stays high, fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_03a | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 0, a pad's output shall be 0. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode); [Sleep Features](../programmers_guide.md#sleep-features) | `pad_sleep`: *tie low in sleep* | While the status bit is 1 and the mode taken at the entry is 0, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 0 in the same cycle. A pad that still carries its peripheral or its select's drive fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_03b | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 0, a pad's output enable shall be 1, so the pad drives 0. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode); [Sleep Features](../programmers_guide.md#sleep-features) | `pad_sleep`: *tie low in sleep* | While held in mode 0, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 1. A pad left high-Z, or following its peripheral's enable, fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_04a | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 1, a pad's output shall be 1. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode) | `pad_sleep`: *tie high in sleep* | While the status bit is 1 and the mode taken at the entry is 1, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 1 in the same cycle. A pad that still carries its peripheral or its select's drive fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_04b | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 1, a pad's output enable shall be 1, so the pad drives 1. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode) | `pad_sleep`: *tie high in sleep* | While held in mode 1, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 1. A pad left high-Z, or following its peripheral's enable, fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_05a | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 2, a pad's output enable shall be 0: the pad is high-Z. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode) | `pad_sleep`: *high-Z in sleep* | While the status bit is 1 and the mode taken at the entry is 2, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 0 in the same cycle. A pad that keeps driving in sleep fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_05b | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 2, a pad's output shall be 0. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode) | `pad_sleep`: *high-Z in sleep* | While held in mode 2, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 0. A pad that leaves its peripheral's data or 1 on its output fails it. |
| REQ_SLP_06a | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 3, a pad shall keep the output it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode); [Retention Logic](../theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic) | `pad_sleep`: *keep holds* | While the status bit is 1 and the mode taken at the entry is 3, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with the output it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1. A pad that follows its peripheral or its select, or keeps the value of another cycle, fails it. No specification states which output a JTAG pad that a TAP owned in that last cycle keeps, so the check claims none for it. |
| REQ_SLP_06b | While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 3, a pad shall keep the output enable it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_mode); [Retention Logic](../theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic) | `pad_sleep`: *keep holds* | While held in mode 3, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with the one it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1. A pad that turns high-Z after driving, or starts to drive after being high-Z, fails it. No specification states which enable a JTAG pad that a TAP owned in that last cycle keeps, so the check claims none for it. |
| REQ_SLP_07 | Once 1, a status bit shall stay 1 until software writes 0 to it, whatever `sleep_en_i`, the sleep enable and the peripheral do. | [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_status${on(topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split(), '_0')}); [Retention Logic](../theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic) | `pad_sleep`: *bit holds until cleared*, *clear releases* | The check _bit holds until cleared_ (CHK_PAD_SLEEP_03) requires a bit at 1 to be 1 in the next cycle unless software clears it, whatever `sleep_en_i`, the sleep enable and the peripherals do; a bit that falls when sleep ends, or on a write of 1, fails it. The check _clear releases_ (CHK_PAD_SLEEP_04) requires a software clear to give 0 in the next cycle, so the bit ends at the clear and not later. |
| REQ_SLP_08 | While its status bit is 0, a pad shall drive what it drives awake: an MIO pad what its output select names, a DIO pad the output and output enable of its own peripheral. | [Retention Logic](../theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic); [Sleep Features](../programmers_guide.md#sleep-features) | `pad_output`: *tie 0 drives 0*, *tie 1 drives 1*, *select 2 is high-Z*, *drives selected output*, *no output is high-Z*, *DIO drives its peripheral* | Each holds in every cycle the pad is awake, its status bit at 0, whether the bit was never set or was cleared; together they cover every select and every DIO pad. A pad that still drives the value of its sleep mode in a cycle its bit reads 0 fails the check of its select; a JTAG pad a TAP owns is decided by the JTAG pad checks. |
