${"##"} Register locks

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: "lock" is one bit of a `*_REGWEN` register; it locks the registers of the same index.
The rule that a locked pad's attributes do not change (`REQ_LOCK_03a`, `REQ_LOCK_03b`) holds except on a JTAG pad while a TAP owns it.

Testpoints: the generated CSR checker (imported testplan), `regwen` (V2, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_LOCK_01a | Every lock shall read 1 after reset. | the register description: the `EN` field of each `*_REGWEN`, e.g. [`MIO_PAD_ATTR_REGWEN.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_attr_regwen) `resval: "1"`, on `clk_i` with `rst_ni` ([pinmux.hjson `clocking`](../../data/pinmux.hjson)); [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format) | generated CSR checker | After reset the generated register checker expects every lock at its reset value 1, bit 31 of `ALERT_TEST` included, and compares each lock's value and read with it; a lock that leaves reset at 0 fails the first compare. |
| REQ_LOCK_01b | Once software writes 0 to a lock, the lock shall stay 0 until reset. | [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format); [Pad Attributes](../programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes) | generated CSR checker | The generated register checker predicts each lock as `rw0c`: an accepted write of 0 clears it and nothing sets it; a lock that returns to 1 before a reset fails the compare. |
| REQ_LOCK_01c | A write of 1 to a lock that is 0 shall not reopen it. | the register description: each lock `rw0c`; [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format); [Pinmux Configuration](../programmers_guide.md#pinmux-configuration) | generated CSR checker | The generated register checker predicts each lock as `rw0c`, which keeps a closed lock at 0 over a write of 1; a lock that such a write reopens fails the compare. |
| REQ_LOCK_02 | While a lock is 0, a write to a register it locks shall leave that register unchanged. | [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_REGWEN.EN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel_regwen); [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format) | `regwen`: *locked read-back holds* | The generated register checker holds each register whose lock reads 0 over every write to it; a register that takes such a write fails it. The attribute registers, whose value the pinmux supplies, are decided by _locked read-back holds_ (CHK_REGWEN_02) on every pad, a JTAG pad a TAP owns included: a locked attribute register whose read-back changes fails it. |
