| REQ_LOCK_03b | While a pad's attribute lock is 0, what its attribute register reads back shall not change. | [`MIO_PAD_ATTR_REGWEN.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_attr_regwen); [Pad Attributes](../programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes) | `regwen`: *locked read-back holds* | It compares what the pad's attribute register reads back in each cycle its lock is 0 with the read-back in the next cycle, on every pad, a JTAG pad a TAP owns included. A locked register that takes a write, whole or in part, fails it. |

${"##"} Register block and bus

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: A "failed request" is a request whose command integrity code does not match, or a write whose data integrity code does not match ([Usage of User Bits](../../../../../ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits): the data code covers "the write data").
A read whose only mismatch is in its data code is not a failed request, and no row checks its response or its alert.
The "in-band reset" is the alert handler's re-initialization, during which it puts a signal integrity error on its ping and acknowledge pairs on purpose ([Employed Solution](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)).
The sender's answer to it, a signal integrity error on `alert_tx_o` and then a return to idle ([Employed Solution](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)), has no row: the sender is the shared primitive `prim_alert_sender` (`rtl/pinmux.sv`:143-147), whose own upstream FPV drives the in-band reset and checks the return to idle (`hw/ip/prim/fpv/tb/prim_alert_rxtx_*`, `InBandInitFromReceiverToSender_A`).
The alert rows read `alert_tx_o`, with an alert handler.
An "illegal combination of address, size and mask" is a request whose address, size and mask do not correspond as TileLink requires (TileLink 1.9.3 p. 49-51: "a_size, a_address and a_mask are required to correspond with one another"): an address not aligned to its size (p. 51: "a_address must be aligned to a_size"), a size above 2, a mask bit set on a byte lane outside the access, or a `PutFullData` whose mask leaves a lane of the access 0.
[Explicit Error Cases](../../../../../ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases) lists the last three "for example"; the unaligned address is verification's reading.

Testpoints: the generated CSR checker (imported testplan), `bus` (V2, priority 2), `alert` (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_REG_01a | Every register field shall take software's reads and writes as the access type of its register description entry says, for every request not answered with an error and, for a write, while the lock of its register reads 1 or it has no lock. | the register description: each field's `swaccess`, e.g. [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_status${on(topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split(), '_0')}) `swaccess: "rw0c"`; [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format) | `pad_attr`: *read-back changes only on a write* | The generated register checker predicts each field from its access type and each request whose integrity codes are correct, and compares the field and every read with it; a field that takes a write its type or a closed lock refuses fails it. The attribute registers keep no value of their own (the pinmux supplies it), so their storage is decided by _read-back changes only on a write_ (CHK_PAD_ATTR_10): a read-back that changes with no accepted write to the pad's attribute register before it fails it. A write refused for its integrity code and the hardware set of a sleep status bit are left to the pinmux's own bus and sleep checks. |
| REQ_REG_01b | Every register field shall read its register description reset value after reset. | the register description: each field's `resval`, e.g. [`MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN`](../registers.md#mio_pad_sleep_status${on(topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split(), '_0')}) `resval: "0"`; [Configuration and Register Definition File Format](../../../../../../util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format) | generated CSR checker | After reset the generated register checker expects each field at its reset value; a field that leaves reset with another value fails the first compare. The attribute registers, whose value the pinmux supplies, are left to _reset attributes_ (CHK_PAD_ATTR_09). |
| REQ_BUS_01a | The pinmux shall answer every request with one response, and only one. | TileLink 1.9.3 p. 39: "Receipt of request messages must result in the eventual receipt of a response message by the requestor."; p. 30: "it is illegal to receive a response without receiving the request."; p. 46: "In TL-UL, every message fits within a single beat" | `bus`: *device rules* | The TL-UL VIP's device rules match each response on the pinmux's port to an open request. A request left without a response, or a second response to one request, fails them. |
