${"##"} USB wakeup

Conditions: The module is usbdev's AON/Wake module, placed in the pinmux as usbdev is not in the AON power domain ([USB Wakeup Detection Module](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#usb-wakeup-detection-module)); what it does is usbdev's spec and testbench (`REQ_USB_06`), and the other rows check how it is connected.
A pinmux port and a port of the module have the same role when usbdev's docs give the module's port the job of the port the top connects to the pinmux port:

Testpoints: `usb_conn` (V2, priority 2), `usb_module` (V2, priority 2).

