${"##"} Strap sampling

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: The TAP straps are seen through the TAP that connects; full reset and NDM reset: terms.
Life cycle conditions follow the life cycle definition table ([Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)), after the delay before a life cycle input counts.${eg(" The pads named are Earlgrey's.", '')}

Testpoints: `strap` (V2S, priority 1).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_STRAP_01 | At each `strap_en_i` pulse while `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0, TAP strap 0 shall take ${eg("pad IOC8's value (MIO 30)", "its pad's value")}, in every life cycle state. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap0`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `strap`: *pulse samples the straps* | ${eg('At every strap pulse with `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` at 0, whatever the life cycle inputs, the check compares strap 0 in the next cycle with MIO 30 (IOC8) of the pulse cycle or of the cycle after it: the one value where the pad holds it in both cycles, either value where the two differ. A strap 0 that misses the pulse, or takes another pad or a value from neither cycle, fails it.', 'Not written for this top.')} |
| REQ_STRAP_02a | At each `strap_en_i` pulse while `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0, TAP strap 1 shall take ${eg("pad IOC5's value (MIO 27)", "its pad's value")} if the live `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is On. Where both straps sample their pads while `lc_dft_en_i` is On and `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0 (`REQ_STRAP_03`), that sampling takes precedence. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap1`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states) | `strap`: *pulse samples the straps* | ${eg('With `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` at 0 and `lc_hw_debug_en_i` On for the two cycles before the pulse, the check compares strap 1 in the next cycle with MIO 27 (IOC5) of the pulse cycle or of the cycle after it, the one value where the pad holds it in both; a strap 1 that keeps its old value fails it. While `lc_dft_en_i` is On the strap follows its pad instead, which _straps follow the pads_ (CHK_STRAP_02) decides.', 'Not written for this top.')} |
| REQ_STRAP_02b | At each `strap_en_i` pulse, TAP strap 1 shall keep its value if the live `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is not On. Where both straps sample their pads while `lc_dft_en_i` is On and `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0 (`REQ_STRAP_03`), that sampling takes precedence. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap1`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states) | `strap`: *pulse samples the straps* | ${eg('With `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` at 0 and neither `lc_hw_debug_en_i` nor `lc_dft_en_i` On in the two cycles before the pulse, the check asserts strap 1 unchanged in the next cycle, whatever IOC5 carries. A PROD chip whose strap 1 takes its pad fails it.', 'Not written for this top.')} |
