${"##"} Latched debug enable

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: The latch, On and Off are as terms defines them.

Testpoints: `latch` (V2S, priority 1).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_DBG_01a | At each `strap_en_i` pulse, the latch shall take On if `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is On. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *pulse samples debug enable* | At a strap pulse with `lc_hw_debug_en_i` On for the two cycles before, `lc_hw_debug_clr_i`, `lc_check_byp_en_i` and `lc_escalate_en_i` at Off for the two cycles before, the check compares `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` with On in the next cycle. A latch that misses the pulse stays Off and fails it. |
| REQ_DBG_01b | At each `strap_en_i` pulse, the latch shall take Off if `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is not On. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *pulse samples debug enable*, *On only at a pulse* | The check _pulse samples debug enable_ (CHK_LATCH_02) compares the output with Off after a strap pulse with `lc_hw_debug_en_i` On in neither of the two cycles before and the three clear inputs at Off. The check _On only at a pulse_ (CHK_LATCH_03) fails any rise to On other than after a strap pulse with the debug enable On in one of the two cycles before, so a latch that follows the debug enable when it turns On later fails too. |
| REQ_DBG_02 | With no `strap_en_i` pulse, no clear and no full reset, the latch shall keep its value, through an NDM reset too. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *latch holds* | With no strap pulse, `lc_hw_debug_clr_i`, `lc_check_byp_en_i` and `lc_escalate_en_i` at Off in the two cycles before, the check asserts the output unchanged; a latch that drops, or follows the live debug enable, fails it. The NDM reset half is not covered: resets after the start of the run are out of scope. |
| REQ_DBG_03 | `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` at any value other than Off shall turn the latch Off. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [lc_ctrl.hjson `inter_signal_list` lc_hw_debug_clr](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/data/lc_ctrl.hjson); [HW_DEBUG_CLR](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/theory_of_operation.md#hw_debug_clr); [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *clear turns Off* | The check compares the output with Off in the cycle after `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` has been at any value other than Off, On included, for two cycles. A latch that stays On, or clears only at On, fails it. |
| REQ_DBG_04 | `lc_check_byp_en_i` at any value other than Off shall turn the latch Off. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *clear turns Off* | The check compares the output with Off in the cycle after `lc_check_byp_en_i` has been at any value other than Off, On included, for two cycles. A latch that stays On through a life cycle transition, or clears only at On, fails it. |
| REQ_DBG_05 | `lc_escalate_en_i` at any value other than Off shall turn the latch Off. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *clear turns Off* | The check compares the output with Off in the cycle after `lc_escalate_en_i` has been at any of its 15 values other than Off for two cycles. A latch that ignores an escalation, or clears only at On, fails it. |
| REQ_DBG_06 | `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` and `lc_check_byp_en_i` at Off shall not turn the latch Off. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *latch holds*, *pulse samples debug enable* | With `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` and `lc_check_byp_en_i` at Off, _latch holds_ (CHK_LATCH_05) asserts the output unchanged outside a strap pulse and _pulse samples debug enable_ (CHK_LATCH_02) asserts On after a pulse with the debug enable On. A latch cleared by an Off value fails one of them. |
| REQ_DBG_07a | `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` shall be On while the latch is On. | [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` PINMUX_HW_DEBUG_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *output On or Off*, *pulse samples debug enable*, *latch holds* | The latch is seen only on `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o`: _pulse samples debug enable_ (CHK_LATCH_02) and _latch holds_ (CHK_LATCH_05) compare it with On after an On sample and while held, and _output On or Off_ (CHK_LATCH_06) rejects the 14 other encodings. An output that shows anything but On while the latch is On fails one of them. |
| REQ_DBG_07b | `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` shall be Off while the latch is not On. | [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` PINMUX_HW_DEBUG_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *output On or Off*, *On only at a pulse*, *clear turns Off* | The check _output On or Off_ (CHK_LATCH_06) rejects every value but On and Off, _On only at a pulse_ (CHK_LATCH_03) any On the latch did not take at a strap pulse, and _clear turns Off_ (CHK_LATCH_04) anything but Off after a clear. An output at another encoding, or On while the latch is Off, fails one of them. |
| REQ_DBG_08 | After a full reset, the latch shall be Off until the next `strap_en_i` pulse. | [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [lc_ctrl.hjson `inter_signal_list` lc_hw_debug_en](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/data/lc_ctrl.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *Off from full reset*, *On only at a pulse* | The check _Off from full reset_ (CHK_LATCH_01) asserts Off in every cycle of a full reset, and _On only at a pulse_ (CHK_LATCH_03) fails any rise to On before a strap pulse with the debug enable On. Together they keep the output Off from the reset to the next pulse. |
| REQ_DBG_09 | A clear in the cycle of a `strap_en_i` pulse shall leave the latch Off. | [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `latch`: *clear turns Off* | The check covers a clear at the strap pulse too: with `lc_hw_debug_clr_i`, `lc_check_byp_en_i` or `lc_escalate_en_i` at a value other than Off for the two cycles before the pulse, the output must be Off in the next cycle even with `lc_hw_debug_en_i` On. A latch where the sample wins over the clear fails it. A clear that begins in the pulse cycle is not decided, as no specification states how soon a clear acts. |
