${"##"} TAP selection and the JTAG pads

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: The JTAG pads are ${eg('IOR3 TCK, IOR0 TMS, IOR2 TDI, IOR4 TRST_N, IOR1 TDO (MIO 38, 35, 37, 39, 36; ', 'the pads the top description assigns to TCK, TMS, TDI, TRST_N and TDO (')}[top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson)).
The rows hold once the straps and life cycle inputs have held for the delay of the input synchronizers; which reset drives a connected TAP's TRST_N in scan mode is open (`REQ_TAP_13`).
A connected TAP: terms.

Testpoints: `jtag` (V2S, priority 1), `jtag_pad` (V2S, priority 2), `jtag_ndm` (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_TAP_01a | With TAP straps 01, `lc_jtag_o` shall carry TCK from its pad, in every life cycle state. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.lc_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads* | ${eg('With TAP straps 01 the life cycle TAP is connected in every life cycle state, and the check compares the `tck` field of `lc_jtag_o` with MIO 38 (IOR3) in the same cycle, in scan mode too. A TCK from another pad, a cycle late or blocked by the life cycle state fails it.', 'Not written for this top.')} |
