${"##"} RRAM TAP

Security-relevant: a security claim depends on these requirements.

Conditions: A top with the RRAM TAP ([top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) `enable_rram_tap`; `top_${topname}.hjson`:1812-1813); a top without it has no row here, and its TAP straps 00 select no TAP ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation)).
The RRAM TAP's port is `rram_jtag`, wired to `rram_macro` ([Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rv_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson), [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect.lc_ctrl.lc_dft_en`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson)).
`RRAM_JTAG_SEL` is a 4-bit multi-bit `rw` field with no lock and reset value `kMultiBitBool4False` ([`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel)); the register rows `REQ_REG_01a` and `REQ_REG_01b` cover its access and reset value.
No doc names the reset that clears it; verification infers `rst_ni`, the reset of the main clock `clk_i` ([pinmux.hjson `clocking`](../../data/pinmux.hjson)).
The JTAG pad rows of hold for the RRAM TAP too: it is a connected TAP (terms).
The rows hold once the straps and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` have held for the delay of the input synchronizers.

Testpoints: `rram_tap` (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement | Sources | Checked by | Why the checks prove it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| REQ_RRAM_01 | With TAP straps 00, `rram_jtag_o` shall carry the four input pads while `RRAM_JTAG_SEL` is `kMultiBitBool4True` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` is On. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` TAP.MUX.LC_GATED](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rram_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `rram_tap`: *connected RRAM TAP gets the pads* | ${eg('With TAP straps 00, `RRAM_JTAG_SEL` at `kMultiBitBool4True` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` On for the two cycles before, the check compares the four fields of `rram_jtag_o` with MIO 38, 35, 37 and 39 in the same cycle. An RRAM TAP left unconnected, fed from another pad or a cycle late fails it.', 'Not written for this top.')} |
| REQ_RRAM_02 | While the RRAM TAP is not connected, `rram_jtag_o` shall carry TMS 0 and TDI 0. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `rram_tap`: *cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0* | In every cycle the RRAM TAP is cut, from the release of `rst_ni` on, the check asserts the `tms` and `tdi` fields of `rram_jtag_o` 0 whatever the JTAG pads carry. It leaves out the cycles in which the TAP is neither connected nor cut, the two after `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` changes and those after a strap sample taken in such a window, as no specification gives how soon a life cycle input or a strap sample acts. A TAP that still sees TMS or TDI from its pads after the straps, the register or `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` deselect it fails it. |
