| REQ_RRAM_07 | `lc_check_byp_en_i` and the latch shall not change whether the RRAM TAP is connected. | [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) | `rram_tap`: *RRAM TAP kept through a transition*, *cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0* | The check _RRAM TAP kept through a transition_ (CHK_RRAM_TAP_05) asserts the request still equal to the JTAG pads while `lc_check_byp_en_i` is not Off or the latched debug enable is Off, and _cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0_ (CHK_RRAM_TAP_02) holds with both free, so neither connects it. A design that cuts the RRAM TAP during a transition, as it cuts the RISC-V TAP, fails the first. |
